==Strategy==
A decently challenging stage featuring the boss, Cat Kart P, who has extremely high damage but also has Single Target. The main threat of the stage comes from getting lucky with your Critical Hitters to remove Metal Doge and Metal One Horn before they become too troublesome. The Angels are unbuffed and can be dealt with using [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist]] and a backliner, or with constant meatshielding if one so happens to not own Artist.

At the start of the level, build up a little bit of money and then kill the Metals with a Critical Hitter, like [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat Sitter,]] or perhaps [[Catyphoon|Hurricat]] if you've managed to obtain him. As tempting as it might seem to do, don't wait out the Angelic Gory.

Upon base hit, Cat Kart spawns, with with a few Angelic Gories and a Metal One Horn walking slowly towards your doom. Lure the Angel threats as well as Cat Kart near your base, then start spamming Artist, your midranger units, and deploy [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] or a backliner Uber to try and kill them as fast as possible. A Metal Doge will also appear among the Angel enemies, so carefully use a Critical Hitter and hope it kills the Metal Doge fast. After that initial rush, you'll usually have to deal with yet another Angelic Gory wave as well as a Metal One Horn. For this phase, there's nothing really that you can do besides keeping a good Critical Hitter stack and hope the Metal One Horn dies fast before too much damage is dealt. This exact wave will happen again after around fifty seconds, and you should do the same thing again.

Once that's done, you're left with only Cat Kart and infinite Metal Doges. Clean them up and victory is yours.

